# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  AI ASSISTANT — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
#
#  Copy to `.env.local` for local development, and set the same variables in
#  your host's dashboard for production (Vercel: Settings → Environment
#  Variables). `.env*.local` is already gitignored.
#
#  EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS SERVER-SIDE. None is prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, which is
#  the only way Next.js puts an environment variable into the browser bundle.
#  If you ever find yourself adding NEXT_PUBLIC_ to a key, stop.
#
#  With none of these set the assistant runs in demo mode: it answers from the
#  knowledge base, costs nothing, and needs no account anywhere.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Option A — Anthropic (best answers, prompt caching, paid) ────────────────
# console.anthropic.com → API keys. Billed per token; see ASSISTANT-README.md
# for what that works out to per month.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Option B — a free tier (no card, works today) ────────────────────────────
# Any OpenAI-compatible provider. Pick one, create a key, uncomment its two
# lines. Set ASSISTANT_OPENAI_MODEL to override the model in assistant.config.ts.
#
#   Groq            console.groq.com/keys
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#
#   Google AI Studio  aistudio.google.com/apikey
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
#
#   Cerebras        cloud.cerebras.ai
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.cerebras.ai/v1
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b
#
#   OpenRouter      openrouter.ai/keys  (models ending in :free)
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#     ASSISTANT_OPENAI_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free
#
# ASSISTANT_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ASSISTANT_OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# ASSISTANT_OPENAI_MODEL=

# ── Lead capture (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where a submitted name and email is POSTed as JSON. Works with a Zapier or
# Make webhook, an n8n endpoint, a Slack incoming webhook, Formspree, a Google
# Apps Script, or your own CRM. Unset: leads are written to the server log.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Optional shared secret, sent as the X-Assistant-Secret header.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Shared rate limiting (optional, recommended on serverless) ───────────────
# Without these, per-IP counters live in each server instance's memory, which
# on serverless means the limit is approximate. Upstash's free tier is ample.
# console.upstash.com → Redis → REST API
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Careers / CV Collection ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# HOW STORAGE WORKS:
#   Local dev  → CVs saved to /data/applications/ on disk
#                Applicant data saved to /data/applications/index.json
#   Production → CVs saved to Vercel Blob (permanent cloud storage)
#                Applicant data saved to Upstash Redis (permanent cloud DB)
#
# You ONLY need the cloud credentials on Vercel. Dev works without them.

# ── Resend (email notifications) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free at resend.com → API Keys. Sends CV-attached notification emails.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...

# Primary inbox that receives new application emails (with CV attached)
# CAREERS_EMAIL=careers@lexoratech.com

# Secondary inbox — also notified on every new application
# CAREERS_CC_EMAIL=hello@lexoratech.com

# ── Vercel Blob (CV file storage) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel Dashboard → Your Project → Storage → Create Blob Store → copy token
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_...

# ── Upstash Redis (applicant metadata) ────────────────────────────────────────
# vercel.com/marketplace → search "Upstash Redis" → add to project
# Then: Vercel Dashboard → Your Project → Storage → Upstash → .env.local
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://...upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...

# ── Admin dashboard password ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Password to log in at /admin/careers — CHANGE THIS before going live!
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=lexora-admin-2026

